      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm seeing some weirdness on subnet 10.42.8.0/24 here in Lyon. Getting reports of intermittent packet loss and really high jitter during peak hours. Here are some traceroute stats from a few different test nodes:\n\n192.168.1.1 -> 10.42.8.1 (avg 2ms)\n10.42.8.1 -> 172.16.5.4 (avg 15ms, spikes to 140ms)\n172.16.5.4 -> 8.8.8.8 (avg 22ms, 5% loss)\n\nThe latency spikes seem to happen at the 172.16.5.4 hop. Can you look at this and tell me if this looks like a physical layer issue or if it's more likely a routing/congestion problem at the edge?",
